    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/c618444fa2d3bb537eceb01bd93d2b8ddf1a70f0</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/zarnthyr/card-janitor/commit/c618444fa2d3bb537eceb01bd93d2b8ddf1a70f0"/>
    <title>
        feat: improves policy related ux
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-16T14:54:16Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/188569615?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>zarnthyr</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/zarnthyr</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat: improves policy related ux

- Duplicate policies.
- Individual-policy JSON editing with Apply/Cancel.
- Line numbers in both JSON editors.
- Unsaved-edit protection.
- Conflict action details and selected-card browsing.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/6423708c529fca3b46a867008a91edc1dcba3cbc</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/zarnthyr/card-janitor/commit/6423708c529fca3b46a867008a91edc1dcba3cbc"/>
    <title>
        fix: improve cleanup reliability and conflict diagnostics
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-16T14:09:10Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/188569615?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>zarnthyr</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/zarnthyr</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix: improve cleanup reliability and conflict diagnostics

- Explain skipped cards with browsable conflict details
- Harden policy validation and stale configuration writes
- Guard automatic cleanup lifecycle and defer opening cleanup until sync
finishes
- Preserve undo recovery after partial cleanup failures
- Optimize evaluation and split editor modules
- Tighten packaging, release tooling, documentation, and regression
coverage&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
